===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{alt form|en|Moodle}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008| title=Creating and Sustaining Small Learning Communities|author=Grace Sammon | page=207| passage=Better yet, take advantage of shared drives, '''moodles''', and blogs as online resources. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011| title=Drama Education with Digital Technology|author=Michael Anderson, ‎David Cameron, ‎John Carroll | page=| passage=We could equally explore the potential of wikis, drupals, '''moodles''' and other software for reflecting on performance making. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013| title=Differentiating By Student Learning Preferences|author=Joni Turville | page=97| passage=Share what has been created in a binder or consider high-tech collaboration tools such as blogs, wikis, or '''moodles'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014| title=Social Work Education and Practice|author=Nikku Bala Raju, ‎Hatta Zulkarnain Ahmad | page=64| passage=The institute continuously strives to host training programs for teachers and students to develop and learn course contents using ''''moodles'''' available for teaching and learning activities.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022| title=Evolutionary Computing and Mobile Sustainable Networks|chapter=Smartphone Usage, Social Media Engagement, and Academic Performance|author=T Ravikumar, R. Anuradha, R Rajesh, and N. Prakash|editor=V. Suma | page=362| passage=The students do not only use smartphones and social media for entertainment, but they use them for information sharing, content sharing, academic peer group discussion, accessing learning websites and applications, and for accessing '''moodles'''.}}

